OVERFLOW — WHEN TO USE LONG LONG
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  int max    ≈  2.1 × 10⁹
  long long  ≈  9.2 × 10¹⁸

  Use long long when:
    - Values can reach 10⁹ and you multiply two of them
    - Summing n values each up to 10⁹  (sum can reach 10¹⁴)
    - Computing factorials beyond 12!  (12! ≈ 4.8 × 10⁸, 13! overflows int)
    - Any intermediate product in modular arithmetic

  // Multiplication — cast BEFORE multiplying, not after
  long long product = (long long)a * b;    // correct
  long long product = (long long)(a * b);  // WRONG — already overflowed

  // Factorial overflow reference
  12!  =  479001600      fits in int
  13!  =  6227020800     overflows int, fits in long long
  20!  =  2.4 × 10¹⁸    fits in long long (barely)
  21!  overflows long long — use modular arithmetic
